209        /* STAT-GEE-009: GEE — STORE
210         * Source: S154 / Chapter 50 / `STORE Statement` (PDF pp. 3443–3444).
211         * Discriminates: Save the fitted item store and inspect it through PROC PLM SHOW ALL.
212         */
213        options nosyntaxcheck obs=max firstobs=1 nodate nonumber nocenter linesize=160 pagesize=max nostimer nofullstimer validvarname=v7
213      ! validmemname=compatible locale=en_US;
214        %let syscc=0;
215        title; footnote;
216        ods _all_ close;
217        ods listing gpath="%sysfunc(pathname(work))";
218        ods graphics off;
219        proc datasets library=work kill nolist;
NOTE: Deleting WORK.CHILDREN (memtype=DATA).
NOTE: Deleting WORK.REGSTRY (memtype=ITEMSTOR).
NOTE: File WORK.REGSTRY (memtype=ITEMSTOR) cannot be deleted because it is in use.
NOTE: Deleting WORK.TEMPLAT (memtype=ITEMSTOR).
NOTE: File WORK.TEMPLAT (memtype=ITEMSTOR) cannot be deleted because it is in use.
NOTE: Deleting WORK._ORACLE_INPUT (memtype=DATA).
219      !                                         quit;


220        ods path work.templat(update) sashelp.tmplmst(read);
221        
222        data Children;
223        input ID City$ @@;
224        do i=1 to 4;
225        input Age Smoke Symptom @@;
226        output;
227        end;
228        datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.CHILDREN has 100 observations and 6 variables.

254        ;
255        proc gee data=Children descending;
256        class ID City;
257        model Symptom = City Age Smoke / dist=bin link=logit;
258        repeated subject=ID / type=exch covb corrw;
259        
260        store out=work._oracle_store;
261        run;

NOTE: PROC GEE is modeling the probability that Symptom='1'.
NOTE: The GEE procedure generated the model item store WORK._ORACLE_STORE.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE GEE printed page 8.

